<title>SLOVAKIA: Slovak statistical bureau details H1, Q2 GDP.</title>
<headline>Slovak statistical bureau details H1, Q2 GDP.</headline>
<dateline>BRATISLAVA 1996-09-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Slovak Statistical Bureau (SUSR) on Wednesday released details of gross domestic product (GDP) for the second quarter and first half of 1996, the main results of which were reported earlier in the day:</p>
<p> GROSS DOMESTIC PRODUCT	 H1'96   Q2'96   Q1'96   Q2'95</p>
<p> real change yr/yr (pct)	+7.1    +6.9    +7.3    +7.1</p>
<p> absolute amount (skk bln)   219.3   113.5   105.8   106.2</p>
<p>(pct change)</p>
<p> household demand		 +7.8    +8.2    +7.4    +7.0</p>
<p> state administration demand +23.7   +13.7   +32.4    +0.5</p>
<p> fixed capital creation	+27.0   +27.8   +25.9    +7.1</p>
<p> exports of goods/services    -6.5    -6.5    -6.6    +2.3</p>
<p> imports of goods/services    +9.9    +3.7   +16.9   +13.9</p>
<p>Note. No compareative figures for the first half of 1995 were available.</p>
<p>-- Tatiana Vacova, Bratislava Newsroom, 42-7-210-3687</p>
</text>
